course: dictionary
lesson: 14387
title: Orthography: the rules of writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Orthography is the system a language uses to write words down. It tells you which letters stand for which sounds, and when to use capital letters, hyphens and punctuation. Think of it as the rulebook for writing.
explain: «Our class is learning English orthography this week.» Here orthography means the rules of English spelling and writing. In everyday talk, people often use it to mean correct spelling, so «Her orthography was excellent» means she spelled the words correctly.
explain: English orthography is famous for being tricky. «Though», «through», «tough» and «cough» end the same way in spelling but sound different. Other languages, like Finnish and Spanish, have more regular orthography, so their spelling follows the sounds more closely.
fact: Orthography is the system of spelling and writing a language.
fact: Orthography covers which letters stand for which sounds, and rules for capital letters, hyphens and punctuation.
fact: «Orthography» can also mean correct spelling.
fact: English orthography is tricky: «though», «through», «tough» and «cough» are spelled alike but sound different.
fact: UK and US orthography differ, so «colour» is UK spelling and «color» is US spelling.
exercise: «Orthography» means what? | *The system of spelling and writing a language | The sound a letter makes when you read it aloud | A very old map of a town | A type of hard stone
exercise: Why is English orthography tricky? | Every English word is spelled exactly as it sounds | English has no letters | *Some words are spelled alike but sound different, like «though» and «tough» | English uses only capital letters
exercise: Which spelling is the UK orthography for the word colour? | color | *colour | colr | kolour
test: Which sentence follows English orthography for capital letters? | *«Today we visited London.» | «today we visited London.» | «today we visited london.»
test: Which word shows a spelling pattern that does not match its sound? | *tough | sun | cat | dog
exam: Which sentence about orthography is true? | *English orthography can be tricky, because some words spelled alike sound different | Every language has exactly the same orthography | Orthography is only about drawing letters neatly | Orthography means reading out loud very fast
